+
+## Diff (JSON Patch generation)
+
+`createPatch(from, to)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, returns a JSON Patch (RFC 6902) that turns `from`
+into `to` when passed to `applyPatch`.
+
+- The patch describes only what differs: objects are compared member by member, arrays element by
+  element after trimming their common start and end, and any other value (or a change of type) is
+  a `replace`. Equal documents give `[]`; a change at the root is a `replace` of `""`.
+- It emits only `add`, `remove` and `replace`; it does not detect moves or copies.
+- The inputs are never mutated and the patch shares no structure with them.
+- `TypeError` when `from` or `to` is not a JSON value (`undefined`, functions, `NaN`/`Infinity`,
+  sparse array holes...). Member names are escaped (`~0`, `~1`); `__proto__` is an ordinary name.
